# Prime review — desk-state contextual Colab 05.01

Date: 2026-10-29. Reviewer: Codex Prime.
Status: answered; implementation correction pending on 0508.return-capture/05.20.

## Outcome, evidence and scope

The return is useful informed self-critique. The recipient authored the original
module and explicitly disclosed it. This is not blind independent certification.
Capture 0168 freshly verified complete. The readable return is byte-identical to
its sealed return. The Colab did not execute desk-state or its backends.
Prime independently reproduced F02 using only the extracted citations_for function:
two references to the same path/commit with different notes attach the first note
to the second reference. That is a real preservation defect and blocks adoption.

## Findings and dispositions

F01: fix. Print handoff author, recorded-prime-intent kind, source basis and commit
in the default readable view and derived candidate. A copied historical next step
must not sound like a current computed instruction.
F02: fix. Preserve each citation's original note and expected hash together with
its own observation result. Never reuse the first same-path/commit observation for
a different expectation or reason. Include same and conflicting expected hashes.
F03: keep the protective lifecycle logic and add readable review disposition and
terminal state where source-bound. Accepted with terminal null stays open.
F04: preserve. Null worker means unrecorded, not available. Test both surfaces.
F05: fix. Include the source path on unidentified/unprojected return rows.
F06: fix. Capture timestamps, projection time and live-file observation times must
have distinct labels. Historical custody timestamps are not current page freshness.
F07: clarify coverage, not invent a decision. A record cannot clear or resolve a
later decision it never examined. Label the view's declared source scope; do not
promote an empty conflict list into a global absence-of-conflicts claim. The current
AR-01 hold stays outside any proposed historical refresh.
F08: verify the stale-source branch in the bounded correction. A stale binding
stays unprojected and is not silently rewritten. No new global authority logic.
F09: preserve bounds and refusals. Do not drop required evidence to fit an output.
F10: historical command counts are observations of the supplied transcript, not a
fresh run or demonstrated time saving. Preserve that distinction in the return.

## Learning and next action

The JSON largely preserves uncertainty, but a concise readable surface can lose
the attribution that made the data safe to interpret. Mechanical preservation must
survive projection into the text people actually read. One bounded repair of that
projection and citation attachment follows. Independent Prime adoption review still
comes after the Builder return. No 00.live rewrite, migration, dispatch, model
handover, current worker-availability claim or Director decision is created here.
